WEBVTT

00:35.782 --> 00:39.621
Now, remember, don't touch this money
until you get to the grocery store.

00:39.830 --> 00:43.085
Then buy one can of beans and come
straight home. Do you understand?

00:43.293 --> 00:45.463
Lois, I'm a guy you can trust
with a task.

00:45.672 --> 00:48.134
I'm the one who almost
conquered the dragon's layer.

00:54.894 --> 00:56.020
Ah!

00:57.064 --> 00:59.150
<i>"Dragon's Layer"</i>

01:04.366 --> 01:05.952
Peter, where have you been?

01:06.160 --> 01:07.997
You left for the market six hours ago.

01:08.247 --> 01:10.625
- Did you get the beans?
- I got something better.

01:10.876 --> 01:14.088
You know how you always wanted
a real diamond engagement ring?

01:14.631 --> 01:16.008
Oh, my God.

01:16.216 --> 01:19.222
That's right. I bought a horse.

01:19.598 --> 01:21.183
You bought a horse?

01:21.392 --> 01:23.979
Why the hell did...?
I didn't give you that much money.

01:24.187 --> 01:25.481
That's what I thought, Lois.

01:25.857 --> 01:28.694
Sold to the gentleman
from Quahog, Rhode Island.

01:28.903 --> 01:31.990
Congratulations, sir.
What brings you down here to Louisville?

01:32.157 --> 01:33.618
I don't know.

01:33.826 --> 01:36.413
Peter, there's something off
about that horse.

01:36.622 --> 01:38.082
You have an eye for animals.

01:38.249 --> 01:41.463
This horse is retarded.
That's why I got it so cheap.

01:42.881 --> 01:45.969
I don't think it's wise
to have a retarded horse as a house pet.

01:46.178 --> 01:51.144
Shut up. You don't know nothing
about anything.

01:51.353 --> 01:53.606
Whatever, Peter. Fine, keep the horse.

01:53.814 --> 01:56.401
Good, this family works much better
when we're unified.

01:56.610 --> 02:00.407
You'll see, this horse
will be a fine addition to our family.

02:01.826 --> 02:04.580
I don't want him to feel self-conscious.
Everybody, pee.

02:04.747 --> 02:07.834
- Peter, we...
- Everybody, pee now.

02:08.043 --> 02:10.421
We're an unusual family.

02:16.555 --> 02:19.645
- Peter, the horse is here.
- Oh, yeah.

02:19.853 --> 02:22.273
It's so creepy,
the way it just stares like that.

02:22.482 --> 02:23.775
Why doesn't it do something?

02:23.983 --> 02:26.112
He's retarded, Lois.
You should understand.

02:26.321 --> 02:28.866
You're married to a retarded man. Eh?

02:29.075 --> 02:31.245
You're married to a retarded man.

02:33.915 --> 02:35.835
Ew! Ew! Ew!

02:36.043 --> 02:39.966
What is it? Brian,
is Paul Sorvino standing behind me?

02:40.174 --> 02:41.801
Hey, you want a sugar cube, horsy?

02:42.052 --> 02:43.846
Oh, God, Brian, don't.

02:46.433 --> 02:50.731
Ugh! Ew! Ew! Ew!

03:02.624 --> 03:06.212
What made you come around, Lois?

03:07.298 --> 03:10.135
I love you so much.

03:10.302 --> 03:13.139
I love you so much, Lois.

03:13.306 --> 03:15.517
I love you too, Peter.

03:17.604 --> 03:20.610
Take Maple Drive, otherwise
we won't make the movie on time.

03:20.818 --> 03:22.905
All right. Uh-oh.

03:23.113 --> 03:24.489
What is it?

03:24.656 --> 03:27.244
The horse is right behind the car.

03:28.454 --> 03:30.248
Peter, that thing is just creepy.

03:30.415 --> 03:33.669
Hey. Scat, scat. Go on, you.

03:33.921 --> 03:36.382
We're go...
We're going to see a movie.

03:36.591 --> 03:38.427
All right,
I'm gonna try something else.

03:48.274 --> 03:50.403
No, no, no!

03:54.618 --> 03:58.832
Oh, that's got
all my stink of the day in it.

03:58.999 --> 04:00.542
That's nasty.

04:05.007 --> 04:07.762
Why are there so many bottles of milk
in the refrigerator?

04:07.971 --> 04:11.267
Thanks for reminding me. Some
of the milk in the fridge is not milk...

04:11.475 --> 04:14.145
...it's horse sperm.
I'm a horse breeder now.

04:24.870 --> 04:26.957
No one's gonna wanna breed
with that horse.

04:27.165 --> 04:28.376
After tomorrow, they will.

04:28.584 --> 04:31.171
I'm gonna enter him in the derby
and he's gonna win.

04:31.380 --> 04:34.217
I just know it.
I got a sixth sense about this things.

04:34.384 --> 04:37.055
<i>Remember when I predicted the ending
to Wild Hogs?</i>

04:37.264 --> 04:39.475
This movie's gonna suck.

04:45.400 --> 04:46.777
Hey there, little fella.

04:46.986 --> 04:48.447
I'm 48.

04:48.655 --> 04:51.994
This whole place is a giant mindfuck.

04:52.202 --> 04:53.830
I've never been in the owner's box.

04:54.039 --> 04:56.333
We are gonna get a great view
from up here.

04:56.542 --> 04:58.879
This is gonna be a great race.

04:59.129 --> 05:01.466
Hey, wha...?
What are you doing? Get down there.

05:01.675 --> 05:04.220
- Where's your midget?
- Sorry, boss. Had to pee.

05:04.429 --> 05:06.515
Come on, you.

05:06.891 --> 05:08.184
Guess he's got a small bladder.

05:09.603 --> 05:12.023
A little tiny guy.
Gotta go all the time.

05:12.231 --> 05:15.153
Even though he's gotta race,
he couldn't hold it.

05:18.073 --> 05:20.912
<i>And they're off.
- Go, horsy, go.</i>

05:21.120 --> 05:23.582
God, it even runs like it's messed up
in the head.

05:27.713 --> 05:31.177
Is there a reason all the horses
are named after cancelled Fox shows?

05:31.385 --> 05:33.680
<i>Kitchen Confidential,
The Wedding Bells...</i>

05:33.889 --> 05:36.351
<i>...followed by Happy Hour,
The War at Home, Drive...</i>

05:36.559 --> 05:39.146
<i>...followed by The Winner,
Life on a Stick, The Loop...</i>

05:39.355 --> 05:41.817
<i>...followed by Head Cases,
Standoff, Vanished...</i>

05:42.025 --> 05:44.863
<i>...followed by Free Ride,
Method & Red, Tru Calling...</i>

05:45.030 --> 05:47.450
<i>...followed by Quintuplets,
Stacked, Justice...</i>

05:47.659 --> 05:49.370
<i>...North Shore, Back to You.</i>

05:49.579 --> 05:52.750
<i>And bringing up the rear
but still in the race is 'Til Death.</i>

05:52.959 --> 05:55.420
- You named your horse "'Til Death"?
- You know why?

05:55.629 --> 05:59.176
Because I'm gonna take this horse
and shove it down America's throat.

05:59.385 --> 06:01.972
<i>What's this?
'Til Death has taken a right turn...</i>

06:02.180 --> 06:03.432
<i>...and is heading into the stands.</i>

06:04.893 --> 06:07.397
<i>I could describe
the horror I am witnessing...</i>

06:07.605 --> 06:11.486
<i>...but it is so ugly and heartrending
that I cannot bring myself to do so.</i>

06:11.736 --> 06:14.407
<i>Although I do possess
the necessary descriptive powers.</i>

06:14.615 --> 06:17.869
<i>Well, at least the horse ran past
the class of deaf second graders.</i>

06:18.120 --> 06:19.748
<i>Oh, no, dear God, he's going back!</i>

06:21.251 --> 06:24.005
<i>Oh, I know you can't hear any screams,
but I assure they are signing frantically...</i>

06:24.171 --> 06:26.925
<i>...just as fast as their fingers
can shape the phonemes...</i>

06:27.134 --> 06:29.053
<i>...necessary
to convey dread and terror.</i>

06:29.262 --> 06:31.933
Wait. Hold the phone,
he's going back toward the track.

06:32.100 --> 06:33.685
Fellas, this race ain't over yet.

06:35.104 --> 06:37.441
Oh, my baby's dead!

06:37.649 --> 06:38.651
It's over.

06:44.576 --> 06:47.330
One hundred thousand dollars'
worth of damage...

06:47.581 --> 06:49.291
...all thanks to that stupid horse.

06:49.541 --> 06:52.047
Can we not talk about the horse, please?
It's gone.

06:52.255 --> 06:56.177
It suffered a heart attack from the
excitement, and I disposed of it properly.

07:07.193 --> 07:08.362
Oh, boy.

07:08.570 --> 07:09.613
I miss the old days...

07:09.821 --> 07:13.410
...when it was just a flaming bag
of poop and a hurtful note.

07:13.619 --> 07:16.206
I have no idea
how the hell we're gonna pay for this.

07:16.414 --> 07:20.546
Well, I'll just have to get a second job
or something. Hand me the classifieds.

07:20.713 --> 07:24.677
Hey, Lois, look at this.
"Subject wanted for medical... "

07:24.886 --> 07:26.680
- What's that?
- "Experiments. "

07:26.847 --> 07:28.016
Exparagus.

07:28.225 --> 07:29.601
Experiments.

07:29.768 --> 07:31.813
Experiments.

07:32.021 --> 07:33.023
Right.

07:33.232 --> 07:36.111
And it says they'll pay handsomely.
This is perfect.

07:36.319 --> 07:38.864
I won't have to take that job
as Matt Damon's neck.

07:39.282 --> 07:40.867
Hey, Matt.

07:41.076 --> 07:42.120
Matt.

07:42.328 --> 07:46.084
Is this one of those movies where you're
an educated Boston street tough?

07:46.292 --> 07:50.257
- I don't have to take that crap from you.
- You have to, my friend. I'm your neck.

07:50.465 --> 07:53.554
What are you gonna do choke me?
You'll die if you do that.

07:53.762 --> 07:55.598
Can somebody from Wardrobe
get a scarf?

07:55.807 --> 07:58.352
Oh, I'm still gonna...
I'll just talk louder.

07:59.145 --> 08:01.148
Ben Affleck married Jennifer Garner...

08:01.356 --> 08:03.943
...but you married a bartender
with a kid.

08:04.153 --> 08:05.904
These are facts.

08:09.160 --> 08:10.327
What do I gotta do, doc?

08:10.536 --> 08:12.080
You don't have to do anything.

08:12.247 --> 08:15.251
We're isolating and studying the effects
of various genes.

08:15.419 --> 08:18.923
We're just gonna give you experimental
injections and record the results.

08:19.132 --> 08:21.595
- What's this one?
- We call this the squirrel gene.

08:21.803 --> 08:24.725
It's effects
will become apparent shortly.

08:32.110 --> 08:34.780
- Okay, what's next?
- This is the Seth Rogen gene.

08:34.947 --> 08:37.242
It will give you the appearance
of being funny...

08:37.451 --> 08:40.122
...even though you haven't actually done
anything funny.

08:42.626 --> 08:44.502
Hey, doc,
are we gonna be much longer?

08:44.712 --> 08:47.299
I gotta get some beers with the fellas
before I go out on this date.

08:48.926 --> 08:51.598
How charming and chubby.
I'm rooting for you.

08:53.475 --> 08:56.063
All right, Mr. Griffin.
We're gonna inject you...

08:56.271 --> 08:59.025
...with what we believe we've isolated
as the gay gene.

08:59.192 --> 09:01.403
- I don't understand.
- Well, if we're correct...

09:01.612 --> 09:04.491
...we will have proven
that homosexuality is genetic...

09:04.699 --> 09:06.577
...and not choice or environment.

09:06.786 --> 09:09.457
Are you crazy? I don't wanna
take a chance on being gay.

09:09.624 --> 09:11.167
We'll give you $ 125.

09:11.334 --> 09:12.336
All right, I'll do it.

09:12.544 --> 09:14.631
Boy, you're more persuasive
than James Bond.

09:16.007 --> 09:18.470
Now,
time for some unfinished business.

09:18.679 --> 09:20.055
- No, James.
- Yes.

09:20.263 --> 09:23.228
- No, James.
- Yes, you're going to have sex with me.

09:23.436 --> 09:26.107
- No, James! I don't want to.
- Yes, you do.

09:26.273 --> 09:28.276
- No, I don't.
- Yes, you do.

09:28.485 --> 09:30.780
- No, I don't.
- Yes, you do.

09:30.988 --> 09:32.866
- Okay, yes.
- See that?

09:33.075 --> 09:35.995
Fifty noes and a yes means yes.

09:40.127 --> 09:41.337
Hi.

09:41.546 --> 09:43.424
So how'd
the medical experiments go?

09:43.632 --> 09:45.802
So good, Lois. So good.

09:46.010 --> 09:48.681
I'm gonna squeeze right in here
if my thighs will let me.

09:51.018 --> 09:53.147
Peter, what exactly
did they inject you with?

09:53.355 --> 09:56.526
Oh, all sorts of things.
Hepatitis vaccine, a couple of steroids...

09:56.736 --> 09:59.114
...the gay gene, calcium,
a vitamin B extract.

09:59.322 --> 10:00.866
- What did you say?
- The gay gene.

10:01.032 --> 10:04.329
I assume that's the one you meant,
though it wasn't the last I said...

10:04.538 --> 10:07.667
...when you said, "What did you say?"
It was the most unusual.

10:07.876 --> 10:12.550
Yes, that's the one I meant.
Peter, are you gay?

10:12.758 --> 10:20.019
Guilty.

10:27.405 --> 10:28.491
Did anybody see...

10:28.699 --> 10:32.621
...that absolutely fabulous piece on Fiji
in yesterday's travel section?

10:34.457 --> 10:36.251
I wish I was Beyoncй.

10:36.460 --> 10:40.049
Maybe you should go back and have
that doctor undo whatever he did.

10:40.257 --> 10:41.342
I mean, you're not gay.

10:43.428 --> 10:46.266
- What?
- I said homosexuality is wrong.

10:46.433 --> 10:48.520
Are you...?
Are you being serious right now?

10:48.728 --> 10:50.355
Keep it in the bedroom, you know?

10:50.563 --> 10:53.486
I'm not holding your face
with my heterosexuality.

10:53.694 --> 10:54.820
No, you are not.

10:55.029 --> 10:58.243
Dad, now that you're gay,
I don't have to have sex with you, do I?

10:58.451 --> 10:59.912
Not unless you want to. Oh!

11:06.337 --> 11:08.215
Oh, my muffins are ready.

11:10.927 --> 11:11.929
You made muffins?

11:12.137 --> 11:13.807
Well, it wasn't the muffin fairy.

11:14.015 --> 11:15.308
Or was it?

11:17.813 --> 11:19.106
- Go ahead, try it.
- Peter...

11:19.314 --> 11:21.443
Try it.

11:21.652 --> 11:24.615
Dad, I think Mom's right.
You should go back to that doctor.

11:24.824 --> 11:26.450
Well, now, wait a minute, Meg.

11:26.617 --> 11:27.995
Let's not be too hasty.

11:28.161 --> 11:29.872
These are delicious.

11:30.081 --> 11:33.168
- What's the secret ingredient?
- Spugizakom.

11:33.795 --> 11:35.380
- Ew!
- What?

11:35.588 --> 11:38.051
Oh, you...
Oh, you thought... No, no, no.

11:38.260 --> 11:41.889
Spugizakom, it's a sugar substitute
from the Czech Republic.

11:42.098 --> 11:43.559
That's right. Spugizakom.

11:50.152 --> 11:51.697
All right, I'll say it.

11:51.864 --> 11:53.574
What the hell are you drinking?

11:53.867 --> 11:56.078
A pomtini. It's a pomegranate martini.

11:56.287 --> 11:58.457
<i>I read about them
in the issue of In Style.</i>

11:58.665 --> 12:01.919
They're what Courtney Thorne-Smith
served at her bachelorette party.

12:06.968 --> 12:08.012
Mm.

12:08.804 --> 12:12.643
So you guys feel like watching
the game at my house on Sunday?

12:12.852 --> 12:14.396
- Sounds good.
- That'd be good.

12:14.563 --> 12:16.023
Hey, Quagmire.

12:16.231 --> 12:18.485
- Quagmire.
- Yeah?

12:18.694 --> 12:20.488
I'll be there.

12:20.696 --> 12:23.452
Well, I think I better get going.

12:23.660 --> 12:25.955
Yeah, why don't you and Cleveland
both get going?

12:26.164 --> 12:28.709
Hey, hey, hey, where you guys going?

12:30.962 --> 12:33.549
If we're gonna do this,
we're gonna do it my way.

12:36.638 --> 12:38.808
- Darn it!
- Knock, knock.

12:39.016 --> 12:40.267
What's the problem, champ?

12:40.476 --> 12:42.562
Why is math so hard?

12:42.813 --> 12:44.357
You know, it doesn't have to be.

12:44.524 --> 12:47.277
One trick I used is turning things
into a word problem.

12:47.486 --> 12:51.116
For example, if there are three
glory holes in the bathroom at the club...

12:51.326 --> 12:53.246
...and 28 guys at the circuit party...

12:53.454 --> 12:57.168
...how many rotations of guys will
it take before everybody's had a turn?

12:57.377 --> 12:59.713
- I don't know.
- Nine, with a remainder of Brent.

12:59.922 --> 13:01.131
Oh.

13:01.341 --> 13:03.426
<i>Because Brent can't fit in the glory hole</i>

13:03.636 --> 13:06.056
<i>And that's why we all like Brent</i>

13:08.768 --> 13:11.605
<i>We now return
to That Black Guy Must Be Doing Well...</i>

13:11.814 --> 13:13.775
...Because Everything He Owns
is White.

13:15.820 --> 13:17.447
Hey, how you doing?

13:17.614 --> 13:19.909
Wow. He must be doing well.

13:20.285 --> 13:22.873
Well, here's the new nightie
you picked out for me.

13:23.081 --> 13:24.166
What do you think?

13:24.375 --> 13:26.670
I'm jealous
of Miss Eats-Anything-She-Wants...

13:26.879 --> 13:29.382
...and-Still-Fits-Into-a-Size-Four.
I could scratch your eyes out.

13:31.844 --> 13:35.308
You know, Peter, with all the shopping
and cooking and decorating...

13:35.516 --> 13:38.645
...I have to say I'm really liking
the new you an awful lot.

13:38.854 --> 13:41.942
An awful lot.

13:42.151 --> 13:43.986
What are you doing?

13:44.195 --> 13:46.449
I'm fooling around.

13:46.657 --> 13:49.411
Come on, sweetie.
Let's have some fun.

13:49.620 --> 13:52.124
Lois, I'm gay.

13:52.333 --> 13:55.086
Wait a minute, you mean,
we can't have sex?

13:55.253 --> 13:56.255
No.

13:56.464 --> 13:58.175
But, Peter, we're married.

13:58.342 --> 14:01.346
Tony Randall was married, Lois.
Rock Hudson was married.

14:01.512 --> 14:02.973
Ronald Reagan was married.

14:03.182 --> 14:05.185
Did you reach a missile pact?

14:05.727 --> 14:08.564
Well, you could say that.
There was a missile.

14:08.773 --> 14:11.026
And something definitely got packed.

14:13.530 --> 14:15.074
Did you discuss ICBMs?

14:15.240 --> 14:16.951
Well, I did see a BM.

14:19.288 --> 14:22.293
So would you consider this
a successful summit?

14:22.461 --> 14:25.215
Oh, yes. I summited three times.

14:25.423 --> 14:27.426
Are you finished
with butt-fucking puns?

14:30.430 --> 14:33.476
Just tell me. Is there anything
you can do to remove this gene?

14:33.685 --> 14:35.980
Mrs. Griffin,
it really doesn't work that way.

14:36.189 --> 14:38.066
We wait for the effects to wear off.

14:38.275 --> 14:41.488
- Well, how long will that take?
- A week, a month, a year.

14:41.696 --> 14:44.242
Five hundred twenty-five thousand
six hundred minutes.

14:44.450 --> 14:45.994
<i>Rent, Rent, Rent.</i>

14:46.161 --> 14:48.540
He could be this way
for the rest of his life.

14:48.748 --> 14:51.252
I don't see the big deal.
I like myself this way.

14:51.460 --> 14:54.216
It's a very big deal.
You'll be treated differently...

14:54.425 --> 14:56.928
...just like my Uncle Ray
with a really high-up anus.

14:58.346 --> 15:00.057
I'll be out in a minute.

15:02.811 --> 15:05.732
- So Dad's gonna be gay forever?
- Possibly, Meg.

15:05.941 --> 15:07.944
We're all gonna have
to get used to this...

15:08.153 --> 15:10.448
...and learn to accept your father
for who he is.

15:10.656 --> 15:12.659
Great plan, Lois.
Hey, here's a nutty idea.

15:12.868 --> 15:15.705
Ever read the Bible? Leviticus 18:22.

15:15.872 --> 15:19.544
You're judgmentally quoting Bible verses
and you don't even know how to read.

15:19.752 --> 15:21.297
Welcome to America, Brian.

15:21.714 --> 15:24.844
Hi, everybody. This is Scott.

15:25.052 --> 15:26.805
Oh, who's Scott?

15:27.014 --> 15:28.141
My soul mate, Lois.

15:28.349 --> 15:31.228
I'm here. I'm queer.
Don't get used to it, I'm leaving you.

15:31.437 --> 15:33.273
- What?
- I'm sorry, Lois.

15:33.481 --> 15:35.401
I can't deny who I am any longer.

15:35.610 --> 15:38.113
I am Peter Griffin, homosexual.

15:38.322 --> 15:40.116
And that's how I'm gonna live my life.

15:40.325 --> 15:42.286
Yeah,
I think that's perfectly disgusting.

15:42.494 --> 15:45.165
Every time you do it,
you're basically sodomizing Jesus.

15:45.373 --> 15:46.667
I just wanna point that out.

15:46.876 --> 15:50.047
Chris, you're the man of the house.
Take the lessons I've taught...

15:50.256 --> 15:52.802
...and be the best leader
of this household you can.

15:53.011 --> 15:54.221
I will, Dad.

16:02.107 --> 16:04.778
Oh, God. I miss Peter so much.

16:04.986 --> 16:07.448
Gay or not,
I just wish he was still here.

16:07.657 --> 16:09.868
I miss Dad too, Mom,
but we'll manage somehow.

16:10.077 --> 16:11.454
We're still a family, right?

16:11.663 --> 16:14.166
Yeah, I mean,
we're tighter than an Asian family.

16:15.001 --> 16:17.588
- You doctor yet?
- No, Dad. I'm 12.

16:17.797 --> 16:19.675
Talk to me when you doctor.

16:23.514 --> 16:25.809
I am so gay for you, Scott.

16:26.017 --> 16:28.855
I'm so gay for you, Peter.

16:29.690 --> 16:31.859
- Penis for your thoughts.
- I just...

16:32.068 --> 16:34.071
You complete me, you know that?

16:34.279 --> 16:36.282
You just make me
wanna be a gayer man.

16:36.491 --> 16:39.036
Oh, come here.

16:39.955 --> 16:42.792
- And you don't miss your wife at all?
- Oh, sure I do.

16:42.959 --> 16:45.421
But this is a whole new chapter
in my life, Scott.

16:45.629 --> 16:47.549
And that chapter is all about you.

16:47.757 --> 16:51.138
<i>Oh, Peter. Let's snuggle on the couch
and watch Lifetime.</i>

16:51.346 --> 16:55.185
<i>We now return to
Meredith Baxter in Raped by a Clown.</i>

16:55.394 --> 16:56.479
<i>It was awful.</i>

16:56.688 --> 16:59.233
<i>He made me do things, awful things.
Awful things.</i>

16:59.442 --> 17:00.527
<i>What kinds of things?</i>

17:00.736 --> 17:01.987
<i>I don't even wanna talk about it.</i>

17:05.951 --> 17:08.705
You sure you don't need
any house repairs, Mrs. Griffin?

17:08.913 --> 17:10.875
No, thanks, Rick.
Ever since Peter left...

17:11.083 --> 17:15.631
...our house hasn't been destroyed
by shenanigans on a weekly basis.

17:18.470 --> 17:21.807
God, I feel so bad for Lois.
She really misses Peter.

17:22.016 --> 17:23.811
I wish there was something
we could do.

17:24.020 --> 17:27.108
Well, there is, Brian. I looked into it.
Straight Camp.

17:27.317 --> 17:28.318
Straight Camp?

17:28.526 --> 17:30.446
Yeah, it's where gays go to get cured.

17:30.654 --> 17:31.865
This is dated last year.

17:32.073 --> 17:34.160
Yeah, I just...
I just had it lying around.

17:34.368 --> 17:37.122
I don't know.
It goes against everything I believe in.

17:37.289 --> 17:39.292
At this point,
I'm willing to try anything.

17:46.260 --> 17:48.013
Oh, for the love of penis.

17:55.483 --> 17:57.402
What the...? Where am I?

17:57.611 --> 18:00.908
This is Straight Camp, Peter.
I'm sorry, but I'm doing this for Lois.

18:01.116 --> 18:03.787
By the time you get out,
you'll be back to your old self.

18:03.995 --> 18:05.540
Welcome to Straight Camp.

18:05.748 --> 18:09.127
You've made a choice
to renounce your evil, sinful ways...

18:09.336 --> 18:12.633
...and redeem yourselves in the eyes
of your lord and savior, Jesus...

18:12.841 --> 18:15.595
...who hates many people,
but none more than homosexuals.

18:15.804 --> 18:19.142
And through our carefully structured
program, you will succeed.

18:20.852 --> 18:23.023
All right, men.
This is Harry the homosexual.

18:23.232 --> 18:27.948
- Say hi to everyone, Harry.
- Hi, fellas. I sure do love being gay.

18:28.156 --> 18:31.786
Harry's choice of lifestyle is wrong.
So we're gonna beat him up for it.

18:31.995 --> 18:35.083
Now, take these baseball bats
and get to it.

18:35.875 --> 18:37.878
All right, good so far.

18:38.087 --> 18:40.215
No, no, no.
Don't use the bats like that.

18:40.424 --> 18:42.218
No, don't use them like that either.

18:42.427 --> 18:45.097
All right, look.
Just put them down and use your fists.

18:45.306 --> 18:47.017
No, no. Not like that!

18:48.561 --> 18:51.857
This next exercise will train you
to talk like a straight man.

18:52.065 --> 18:55.780
Peter, we'll start with you. Repeat
every word I say exactly as I say it.

18:55.989 --> 19:00.203
Me and my friends Polly and Matty
are going out to drink a ton of beers.

19:00.412 --> 19:02.040
My friends and I are going out...

19:02.206 --> 19:04.668
...but we're not drinking.
Those are empty calories.

19:04.877 --> 19:08.507
Then we'll play full-contact football
in the park with no pads or helmets.

19:08.716 --> 19:11.553
Then we're gathering at Alan
and Omar's for bad-movie night.

19:11.762 --> 19:14.891
Then it's straight to the bars
to find women to have sex with.

19:15.099 --> 19:17.269
Then it's straight to the gym
for crunches...

19:17.479 --> 19:19.397
...and eye contact with strangers.

19:19.647 --> 19:21.192
- Peter!
- Don't give me that look.

19:21.359 --> 19:23.780
That's what you said.
I said it right back to you.

19:27.952 --> 19:29.205
Oh, excuse me.

19:29.413 --> 19:32.292
I'm sorry to bother you,
but I didn't know where else to go.

19:32.501 --> 19:35.672
I haven't seen Peter in two days
and I thought he might be here.

19:35.881 --> 19:38.009
What? Oh, my God. Peter's missing?

19:38.218 --> 19:39.219
Hey, hang on, hang on.

19:39.427 --> 19:42.516
Before anyone gets too worked up,
I know where Peter is.

19:42.724 --> 19:44.519
- Where?
- I put him in a straight camp.

19:44.685 --> 19:46.772
- You what?
- Oh, you bastard.

19:46.980 --> 19:49.109
Brian, what...? Why did you do that?

19:49.317 --> 19:51.027
It's just you seemed so unhappy...

19:51.237 --> 19:53.991
...and I just wanted to help you
get your husband back.

19:54.200 --> 19:57.287
Who knows? By now, Peter
could be completely heterosexual again.

20:07.302 --> 20:08.971
Stop!

20:09.597 --> 20:11.391
Lois, what are you doing here?

20:11.559 --> 20:15.355
I'm here to get you out of this place,
Peter. I'm taking you back to Scott.

20:15.564 --> 20:18.861
Really? You're not still upset
about my leaving?

20:19.069 --> 20:21.614
There's nothing I'd want more
than to have you back...

20:21.823 --> 20:24.035
...but your place is in Scott now.

20:24.244 --> 20:27.666
I mean, a person's sexual identity
is no more a choice...

20:27.875 --> 20:29.418
...than the color of his skin.

20:29.627 --> 20:33.173
This is who you are,
I can't change you.

20:33.382 --> 20:35.260
And it would be wrong for me to try.

20:35.468 --> 20:39.433
Oh, Lois, you've made me happier
than a pig among guinea pigs.

20:41.019 --> 20:44.648
All right, I think we're all in agreement.
I'm in charge here.

20:48.821 --> 20:49.823
Hi, Peter.

20:50.032 --> 20:51.867
Hi, Scott.

20:53.537 --> 20:56.458
Guess what.
I have a welcome-home surprise for you.

20:56.667 --> 20:58.044
Dish, dish, dish.

20:58.210 --> 20:59.671
Remember how you told me...

20:59.838 --> 21:02.216
...your ultimate fantasy
was to have an 11-way?

21:02.425 --> 21:05.095
Oh, my God, yes, I do,
and you so did not even.

21:05.304 --> 21:06.681
Oh, but I did.

21:06.890 --> 21:08.684
Yoo-hoo! Guys.

21:14.108 --> 21:16.445
Oh, here are my notes
about the gay gene.

21:17.822 --> 21:20.368
It wears off
after two and a half weeks.

21:20.576 --> 21:23.331
Oh, great.
Now I can't find Mrs. Griffin's number.

21:23.540 --> 21:25.334
Okay, everybody ready?

21:25.542 --> 21:27.796
Oh, God,
I feel like a kid in a candy store...

21:28.004 --> 21:30.132
...who's having sex
with a bunch of gay guys.

21:40.231 --> 21:41.524
Wait a minute.

21:41.733 --> 21:43.735
What's going on here?

21:44.028 --> 21:47.282
Holy crap! Ah!

21:49.411 --> 21:50.955
These are mine.

21:51.163 --> 21:52.248
Ah!

21:56.880 --> 21:59.802
So we're just, like,
never gonna talk about this again?

21:59.969 --> 22:01.095
That's right, sweetie.

22:01.303 --> 22:03.890
Well, I'm just happy
to have your father home again.

22:04.100 --> 22:07.479
Yeah, and thank God
everything's back to normal.

22:08.313 --> 22:10.692
Take back your fucking horse!

22:10.693 --> 23:11.693
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru